@startuml
allowmixing
!theme plain
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0

class AuthBoundary <<Boundary>> {
  + submitCredentials()
}
note top of AuthBoundary : Interface for Field Engineer to submit authentication credentials.

class AuthController <<Control>> {
  + validateCredentials()
  + confirmAuthentication()
}
note top of AuthController : Coordinates validation of credentials and confirmation of authentication.

class UserAccount <<Entity>> {
  - userId
  - username
  - passwordHash
  - role
  - status
  - assignedSiteIds
}
note top of UserAccount : Persistent account information for all system users (engineers, administrators).

class SiteListBoundary <<Boundary>> {
  + requestAssignedSites()
}
note top of SiteListBoundary : Provides the Field Engineer with the list of sites assigned to them.

class SiteListController <<Control>> {
  + retrieveAssignedSites()
}
note top of SiteListController : Retrieves and returns the set of sites assigned to a Field Engineer.

class Site <<Entity>> {
  - siteId
  - name
  - location
  - assignedEngineerIds
}
note top of Site : Physical location that can be assigned to engineers and linked to inspection reports.

class ReportDraftBoundary <<Boundary>> {
  + startReportDraft()
  + addChecklistItem()
  + attachPhoto()
  + saveDraft()
}
note top of ReportDraftBoundary : UI/API used by a Field Engineer to create and edit an inspection report draft.

class ReportDraftController <<Control>> {
  + createDraft()
  + addChecklistItem()
  + attachPhoto()
  + saveDraft()
}
note top of ReportDraftController : Coordinates creation of a draft inspection report, checklist handling and photo attachment.

class InspectionReport <<Entity>> {
  - reportId
  - siteId
  - engineerId
  - status
  - checklistData
  - photoIds
  - createdAt
  - submittedAt
  - pdfSummaryId
  - thumbnailIds
  - followUpFlag
}
note top of InspectionReport : Persistent inspection report, may be in draft or submitted state.

class ReportSubmitBoundary <<Boundary>> {
  + submitReport()
}
note top of ReportSubmitBoundary : Interface for a Field Engineer to submit a completed inspection report.

class ReportSubmitController <<Control>> {
  + recordSubmission()
  + generateThumbnails()
  + generatePDF()
}
note top of ReportSubmitController : Handles recording of submission, thumbnail generation and PDF creation.

class Thumbnail <<Entity>> {
  - thumbnailId
  - photoId
  - imageData
}
note top of Thumbnail : Small image derived from a photo attached to an inspection report.

class PDFSummary <<Entity>> {
  - pdfId
  - reportId
  - fileData
}
note top of PDFSummary : PDF document summarising a submitted inspection report.

class ReportBrowseBoundary <<Boundary>> {
  + requestReportList(filters)
}
note top of ReportBrowseBoundary : Provides Site Manager with filtered list of inspection reports.

class ReportBrowseController <<Control>> {
  + retrieveReports(filters)
}
note top of ReportBrowseController : Retrieves inspection reports according to supplied filters.

class PhotoViewBoundary <<Boundary>> {
  + requestPhotos(reportId)
}
note top of PhotoViewBoundary : Allows Site Manager to request photos for a selected inspection report.

class PhotoViewController <<Control>> {
  + retrievePhotos(reportId)
}
note top of PhotoViewController : Fetches photos associated with an inspection report.

class Photo <<Entity>> {
  - photoId
  - reportId
  - imageData
  - metadata
}
note top of Photo : Image captured on site and attached to an inspection report.

class PDFDownloadBoundary <<Boundary>> {
  + requestPDF(reportId)
}
note top of PDFDownloadBoundary : Interface for Site Manager to obtain the PDF summary of a report.

class PDFDownloadController <<Control>> {
  + retrievePDF(reportId)
}
note top of PDFDownloadController : Retrieves the PDF summary for delivery to the Site Manager.

class FlagBoundary <<Boundary>> {
  + flagReport(reportId)
}
note top of FlagBoundary : Allows Site Manager to flag an inspection report for follow-up.

class FlagController <<Control>> {
  + recordFlag(reportId)
}
note top of FlagController : Records the follow-up flag on an inspection report.

class FollowUpRequest <<Entity>> {
  - requestId
  - reportId
  - engineerId
  - status
  - createdAt
}
note top of FollowUpRequest : Request assigned to a Field Engineer after a report is flagged.

class EngineerAccountBoundary <<Boundary>> {
  + manageEngineerAccount(operation, data)
}
note top of EngineerAccountBoundary : Interface for Administrator to create, modify or deactivate engineer accounts.

class EngineerAccountController <<Control>> {
  + validateAccountData()
  + executeAccountOperation()
}
note top of EngineerAccountController : Validates data and executes account-management operations.

class AssignmentBoundary <<Boundary>> {
  + assignEngineerToSite(engineerId, siteId)
}
note top of AssignmentBoundary : Interface for Administrator to assign engineers to sites.

class AssignmentController <<Control>> {
  + recordAssignment()
}
note top of AssignmentController : Records the assignment relationship between an engineer and a site.

class BackupBoundary <<Boundary>> {
  + initiateBackup()
}
note top of BackupBoundary : Triggers the nightly backup process inside the system.

class BackupController <<Control>> {
  + selectData()
  + packageBackup()
  + attachRetentionMetadata()
  + transmitBackup()
}
note top of BackupController : Selects daily reports and photos, packages them, attaches retention metadata and transmits to external storage.

class BackupBundle <<Entity>> {
  - bundleId
  - reportIds
  - photoIds
  - metadata
}
note top of BackupBundle : Aggregated data set containing the day’s reports, photos and metadata for backup.

class BackupServiceInterface <<Boundary>> {
  + receiveBackup(bundle)
}
note top of BackupServiceInterface : External interface used by the system to deliver backup bundles to the Backup Storage Service.

class BackupServiceController <<Control>> {
  + storeBundle()
}
note top of BackupServiceController : Handles acknowledgement and storage confirmation from the external backup service.

Field_Engineer --> AuthBoundary : Field Engineer submits credentials via AuthBoundary.
AuthBoundary --> AuthController : AuthBoundary delegates credential validation to AuthController.
AuthController --> UserAccount : AuthController accesses UserAccount to verify credentials.
Field_Engineer --> SiteListBoundary : Field Engineer requests assigned sites.
SiteListBoundary --> SiteListController : Boundary forwards request to controller.
SiteListController --> Site : Controller retrieves Site entities assigned to the engineer.
Field_Engineer --> ReportDraftBoundary : Field Engineer creates and edits a draft report.
ReportDraftBoundary --> ReportDraftController : Boundary delegates draft operations to controller.
ReportDraftController --> InspectionReport : Controller creates a new InspectionReport in draft status.
ReportDraftController --> Photo : Controller attaches Photo entities to the draft.
Field_Engineer --> ReportSubmitBoundary : Field Engineer submits a completed report.
ReportSubmitBoundary --> ReportSubmitController : Boundary forwards submission to controller.
ReportSubmitController --> InspectionReport : Controller records submission and changes status.
ReportSubmitController --> Thumbnail : Generates thumbnails for attached photos.
ReportSubmitController --> PDFSummary : Generates PDF summary of the report.
Site_Manager --> ReportBrowseBoundary : Site Manager browses inspection reports.
ReportBrowseBoundary --> ReportBrowseController : Boundary delegates browsing to controller.
ReportBrowseController --> InspectionReport : Controller retrieves matching InspectionReport entities.
Site_Manager --> PhotoViewBoundary : Site Manager requests photos of a report.
PhotoViewBoundary --> PhotoViewController : Boundary forwards request to controller.
PhotoViewController --> Photo : Controller retrieves Photo entities.
Site_Manager --> PDFDownloadBoundary : Site Manager requests PDF summary.
PDFDownloadBoundary --> PDFDownloadController : Boundary forwards request to controller.
PDFDownloadController --> PDFSummary : Controller retrieves the PDFSummary entity.
Site_Manager --> FlagBoundary : Site Manager flags a report for follow-up.
FlagBoundary --> FlagController : Boundary delegates flagging to controller.
FlagController --> InspectionReport : Controller sets followUpFlag on the report.
Field_Engineer --> FollowUpRequest : Engineer views assigned follow-up requests after sign-in.
Administrator --> EngineerAccountBoundary : Administrator manages engineer accounts.
EngineerAccountBoundary --> EngineerAccountController : Boundary forwards account-management actions.
EngineerAccountController --> UserAccount : Controller manipulates UserAccount entities.
Administrator --> AssignmentBoundary : Administrator assigns engineers to sites.
AssignmentBoundary --> AssignmentController : Boundary forwards assignment request.
AssignmentController --> Site : Controller records engineerId in Site.assignedEngineerIds.
AssignmentController --> UserAccount : Controller records siteId in UserAccount.assignedSiteIds.
System --> BackupBoundary : Scheduled job triggers nightly backup.
BackupBoundary --> BackupController : Boundary starts backup coordination.
BackupController --> InspectionReport : Selects reports for the day.
BackupController --> Photo : Selects photos for the day.
BackupController --> BackupBundle : Packages selected data into a bundle.
BackupController --> BackupServiceInterface : Transmits bundle to external storage.
BackupServiceInterface --> BackupServiceController : External service acknowledges receipt.
BackupServiceController --> BackupBundle : Controller records the stored backup bundle.

@enduml